Notes

Custom CSS:The index.css file ensures a responsive, polished UI with minimal overrides.
Test the app on different screen sizes to verify responsiveness.

SKU Validation:The /validate-skus route checks each SKU against Shopify’s inventory, logging results and displaying invalid SKUs to the user.
Ensure SKUs in the CSV (e.g., P1-21F-Y) match Shopify’s variant SKUs exactly.

Loading States:The Spinner provides visual feedback during project loading and SKU validation, complementing the ProgressBar.js for CSV parsing and import.

Testing:Test with a sample CSV containing columns like P1-21F-Y Count.
Verify collapsible rows in BackerPreview.js, SKU validation errors in ProductMapping.js, and loading spinners in Dashboard.js.
Check logs/error.log and logs/combined.log for debugging.

Deployment:Run npm run build:frontend to generate frontend/build.
Deploy the backend (e.g., Heroku) and frontend (e.g., Vercel or served via server.js).
Ensure .env includes all required variables (SHOPIFY_API_KEY, AWS_ACCESS_KEY, etc.).
Create the logs/ directory for logging.

